    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0095" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/72<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >1/15</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-04T12:00:00-06:00">June 4, 1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        6:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Department’s cable No. 40, June 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d97-f1"/> I
                    conferred with the President at 11 a.m. He accepted the proposals in their
                    entirety and is anxious to cooperate at the earliest possible date. Please
                    advise as to date of arrival of officers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hornibrook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
